X.append(P(f'with Δ_t in place of Δ. The decay and the rotation are both scaled by the step, as in the standard zero-order-hold discretization of selective state-space models {c("mamba")}. Scaling the rotation is essential: a rotation that is not scaled scrambles the phase of a stored value during a long hold (Figure {FN["gating"]}, Section 6.5). Because the recurrence remains first-order and linear in the state, its evaluation can be parallelized by a scan {c("blelloch","martin")}; the scan agrees with the sequential recurrence to 2.4 × 10⁻¹³. HT-A is bounded when its gain is tied to its step,'))
