X.append(P('and the bound is attained for real poles (50.5 against a bound of 50.5 for h = 50) and approached for complex poles (32.6 at ω = 0.5). The cost of one layer with d channels and N modes per channel is about 14TdN operations for the recurrence, against 4T²d + 5T² for exact attention; the arithmetic crossover is at T ≈ 55. The recurrence needs one complex number per mode and runs in a stream. The FFT form costs O(T log T) per channel. Derivatives with respect to horizons, frequencies and gains are available in closed form through a second recurrence and agree with finite differences. Finally, the response approximately follows the dilation of the input: a burst dilated by a factor a = r = 2 gives coefficients at the next scale that are √a times those of the original at the previous scale.'))
